# Results / artifacts.
#
# CHANGED 2026-09-09: run artifacts ARE now tracked. The project runs on more
# than one machine, and a clone previously arrived with no record of what had
# been run -- no gate verifications, no run metadata, no round or oracle logs,
# no mechanism reports, no analysis output. Anyone (or any agent) picking the
# repo up on a second machine had to be told the state out of band. Tracking
# them makes the repository self-describing: `docs/*_gates.md` says what was
# pre-declared, and `results/` says what happened.
#
# What stays out, and why:
#   *.pt/*.pth/*.ckpt   ~155 MB of training checkpoints. Binary, rewritten
#                       every round, and fully regenerable from the config and
#                       seed -- they would dominate the history while telling a
#                       reader nothing the logs do not.
#   *.npz               raw sampled datasets from closed diagnostics.
#   results/runs/       pilot-era runs from the PRE-G9 source architecture.
#                       Superseded by runs_constraint_batch_g9/g10; kept
#                       locally as history, not evidence for any live claim.
#   g3.../dataset/,     ~81 MB of raw trajectory dumps from finished
#   g8_nonstationary... diagnostics whose conclusions live in docs/g3_gates.md
#                       and docs/g8_gates.md.
#   a3 queue bookkeeping  the per-seed status files, lock files and the atomic
#                       write temporaries. These are LIVE SCHEDULER STATE, not
#                       evidence: `--dry-run` rewrites them, the queue rewrites
#                       them after every run, and `test_a3_queue_isolation.py`
#                       deletes them by fixture. Tracking them meant the
#                       runbook's own pre-flight (run the tests, then the dry
#                       run, then launch) left the tree dirty at the moment of
#                       launch, and `_git_sha` stamps `dirty: true` plus
#                       `dirty_paths` into all twelve production
#                       `run_metadata.json` files. The campaign's real audit
#                       trail is each run's own artifacts -- rounds.jsonl,
#                       run_metadata.json, the gate reports -- all still
#                       tracked. `a3_frozen_verification.json` also stays
#                       tracked: it is a verification RESULT, written once by
#                       `a3_verify_frozen.py`, not scheduler state.
#
# Net effect: ~103 MB tracked, ~232 MB not. A new 250-round run adds ~5 MB.
notebooks/results/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.npz
results/runs/
results/g3_source_diagnostic/dataset/
results/g8_nonstationary_source_diagnostic/
results/runs_a3/a3_queue_status*.json
results/runs_a3/.a3_queue*.lock
results/runs_a3/*.tmp

